Fixes to the F# tokenizer of lizard 1.26.1.

- `$@"` and `@$"` strings are verbatim, but Pygments lexes them as escaped
  ones, so a trailing `\"` swallowed the rest of the file.
- A name with a prime, `id'`, is one token: Pygments leaves the `'` apart.

--- a/lizard_languages/fsharp_tokens.py
+++ b/lizard_languages/fsharp_tokens.py
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 joined, `#` directive lines dropped and each line's first code token
 marked with its column."""
 
+import re
